# Normalise line endings so the repository is byte-identical regardless of which
# platform a contributor is on.
#
# Without this, a clone on Windows checks files out with CRLF and every one of them
# shows as modified on a Mac or in CI — reviews fill up with whole-file diffs that
# contain no actual change, and `git blame` stops being useful.
#
# `text=auto` means: normalise to LF *in the repository*, and check out using each
# platform's native convention. So Windows editors still see CRLF locally; only what
# git stores is normalised.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Files whose content is not line-oriented. Marking them explicitly stops git from
# ever attempting normalisation on them, which would corrupt them silently.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Lockfiles are generated, not written. Collapsing them in diffs keeps a dependency
# bump from burying the code changes it accompanies.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true diff=none
